Z||000000||conductor||12-16-2001||06:36 PM||||When I start my car and drive away there is only a slight hesitation but when I go shopping and I cme back , the car wont start.<BR>It takes sometimes 10 to 12 efforts to get it running. <BR>Because of this I replaced the fuelfilter(the other one was one year old and seemed ok from inside, )<BR>What could be causing this?<BR>Grtx Richard.||||reg||9
Z||000001||GTDude||12-16-2001||08:37 PM||||You need to give us some more information on this one.  It could be almost anything.  My first guess would be the fuel pump, but without more info...there is no way to tell.  Glad to try to help.  I'm a GM auto technician.<P>Phil Pettus<P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||camon||12-17-2001||02:10 AM||||When you turn the key to the on position (not starting the engine) do you hear your fuel pump run (it will sound like a buzz that lasts for 2 seconds) if not their lies the problem. You could also after trying to start the car (and it doesn't start) Try pulling a spark plug and look if the spark plug is wet with gas. If it ain't then it is a fuel related problem (fuel pump, fuel pump relay ect...).<BR>If the plug is wet or you do here the pump run then your problem is more then likely ignition related (coil, control module ect...).<P><BR>Like GTDude said more info would be needed to get board members to help narrow down the problem!<P>------------------<BR>   Keith<BR>1987 Fiero GT||||reg||12
Z||000003||conductor||12-17-2001||09:30 AM||||I replaced the plugs this spring (champion I believe)8.0 accel wires and have the recalls done a few weeks back.<BR>My temp.gauge doesnt work since I bought it 2 years ago. <BR>I have put a lightbulb in the check engine position, was empty(!)<BR>When I came back from the recall,it hesitated in 5th gear when I wanted to accelerate.<BR>At the trafficlight when I want to drive away it wants to die and only if I increase rpms very subtle and slowly it doesnt.<BR>I hope this is enough info so you can help me out.<BR>:-)<BR>Grtx Richard||||reg||1
Z||000004||84Bill||12-17-2001||10:19 AM||||Could be a any number of things. Without knowing what year and engine you have it pretty tricky to diagnose. It sounds like a MAP problem but it could also be the ignition module or pickup coil.||||reg||5
Z||000005||Fie Ro||12-17-2001||10:26 AM||||Richard has the 4 cil......I guess it's an '86||||reg||1
Z||000006||GTDude||12-17-2001||11:35 AM||||Hmmmmmm.....just a guess without more info, but it could just be a stuck open EGR valve or one that is not fully seating.  If you want to check on it....remove the egr valve...only 2 nuts and 1 vac line and see if it is carboned up and not seating or worse yet stuck open.  Hope this helps.<P>Phil Pettus<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gtdude_1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||1
